  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nThe Oxfordshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1895\n£40.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nCompiled and Edited by Captain A. F. Mockler-Ferryman\n\nPublished 1896 - Eyre and Spottiswoode, London\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nRegimental Calendar for 1895\nThe Army List January 1895\nThe Army List December 1895\nThe First Battalion 1895\nRecord of 1st Battalion in 1895\nThe 2nd Battalion in 1895\nRecord of 2nd Battalion in 1895\nThe Depot in 1895\nLetter to the Editor\nSpot the Depot\nExtracts from the London Gazette in 1895\nRoyal Humane Society Medal\nChanges in Equipment\nMusketry\nAthletics\nFootball\nCricket\n2nd Battalion Pony Races in 1895\nOccasional Notes\nSignalling 1895\nThe 43 Light Infantry Dinner in 1895\nThe 52nd Light Infantry Dinner in 1895\n\nMiscellaneous:\nLieut. Colonel Charles MacLeod\nLieut. Colonel Sir Edward Gibbs\nGeneral George Whichcote\nSir James Fergusson\nThe Colours of the Regiment\nWar Medals\nThe Talavera Clasp\nEl Chico Blanco\nDon Miguel Alava\nFrom Private to Adjutant\nPrivate Carney Wood\nA Nautical Adventure\nThe Kaffir War 1851-3 Sergeant Offord's Journal\nA Sergeant’s Letter 1854\nThe annexation of Oude\nReview: Mr Wilberforce’s Munity Story\nNotes from an African Diary\nPig-sticking at Bareilly\nThe Irish Manoeuvres\nSeniority of the Regiments\n\nNotice to Correspondents\n\nIllustrations\n\nMaps\n\n \n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nThe Skipper’s War: Dragon School, Oxford & The Great War\n£20.00 Add to cart\nConflict & County\n£5.95 Add to cart\nA True Soldier Gentleman: The Memoirs of Lt. John Cooke 1791-1813\n£3.95 Add to cart\nBugle & Sabre Magazine – Issue X\n£5.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
